\title[Recession Geometry of Min-Plus Digests]{The Recession Geometry of Min-Plus Digests:\\
Exact Collision Cones, Hitting-Set Duality,\\ and the Collapse of Tropical Hashing}

\author{Aristotle}
\date{20 August 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We give a complete geometric analysis of the fibers of the min-plus (``tropical'') matrix--vector digest
\[
D_A(m)_i \;=\; \min_{1 \le j \le k} \bigl( m_j + A_{ij} \bigr), \qquad A \in \RR^{r \times k},\ m \in \RR^k,
\]
the hash primitive underlying proposals for tropical cryptographic schemes. We determine, for every key and every message, the recession cone of the polyhedral fiber cell through that message.

We prove four groups of results. First, a \emph{universal lower bound}: for every key $A$ and every message $m$, the collision cone at $m$ --- the set of directions $v$ with $D_A(m + sv) = D_A(m)$ for all $s \ge 0$ --- spans a subspace of dimension at least $k - r$. Second, an \emph{exactness theorem in general position}: if each digest component has a unique minimizing coordinate $p(i)$, the collision cone is precisely $\{v \ge 0 : v_{p(i)} = 0\}$, of span-dimension exactly $k - r$ when $p$ is injective; the general-position locus is nonempty for all $r \le k$ and open, with an explicit $g/4$ perturbation bound, and strictness cannot be dropped. Third, a \emph{combinatorial duality}: a coordinate set $S$ may be freely increased without changing the digest if and only if every component retains an active coordinate outside $S$; hence the maximal coordinate collision cone has dimension exactly $k - \tau(A,m)$, where $\tau$ is the minimum size of a hitting set of the family of active sets. We show that the natural transversal (system-of-distinct-representatives) formulation of this criterion is \emph{false}. Fourth, we \emph{refute} the conjectured bounded-alphabet security threshold: for any key with $r < k$ and any two-letter alphabet, two distinct messages collide, with no dependence on any key-spread parameter; the threshold is exactly two letters, and it is sharp in $r$ because $r = k$ admits digests injective on a box. Finally, inversion is a \emph{one-shot test}: the fiber over $y$ is nonempty iff the explicit canonical candidate $m^\star_j = \max_i (y_i - A_{ij})$ lies in it, and likewise under box constraints, so no hardness for constrained tropical mining can originate in the min-plus structure itself.
\end{abstract}

